# Do the two architecture consultations really agree?

**Subject documents:** `dc-warn/out/sol-architecture-consult/ASTRA-ANSWER.md` (86 lines) and `SOL2-ARCH-ANSWER.md` (125 lines), both read in full, against `QUESTION.md`.
**Repository:** `boring-wt-architecture` @ HEAD `e1c6597514…` (read-only; the working tree also carries the 2-line `SwiftArrayBoundary.hx` `render()` fix — verified via `git diff --stat`, see evidence/e06 note).
**Method:** code readings and retained-report readings only. No builds, no tests, no writes outside this directory. Every claim below is labelled **[V]** (I verified it against the repository or a retained executed report) or **[A]** (the document asserts it; I did not establish it).
**Prior cross-check:** `dc-warn/astra-claims-xcheck/REPORT.md` (found one Astra claim IMPRECISE, one under-described). Both of those findings survive this audit and do not change the agreement picture.

